    "updated_at": "2023-01-10T00:01:27Z",
    "body": "> There is a wpt test [fs/FileSystemSyncAccessHandle-close.https.tentative.worker.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/fs/FileSystemSyncAccessHandle-close.https.tentative.worker.html?label=master&label=experimental&aligned) ensuring `close()` is idempotent and I think Chromium does this, but it is not in spec. It would be nice to make it clear.\r\n\r\nThanks for bringing this up, @szewai. And you're correct that `close()` is intended to be idempotent and is implemented as such in Chromium. Amusingly, the current spec language is actually correct on that front (`set this.state to \"closed\"` _is_ idempotent) but this will become _more obviously idempotent_ once we add language to release the lock :)",
